# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the whole module

checkSubset is operation
checkSubset purpose "Check that a modelled module is in the stage0 subset and collect its values, calls, labels, and steps for the emitter"
checkSubset invariant collectsProgram "For a module in the subset, enters every constant, let, and call result in values (constants first), every call in calls, every label in labels with its loop and bound, and every step of main in steps, in source order"
checkSubset invariant rejectsOutsideSubset "A predicate, payload, type, target, or step outside the subset is refused at the word concerned, as is a module with no main"
checkSubset invariant checksTypes "Literals fit their types, arguments match their target's slots, types, and modes, and the values steps name exist with the types the steps need"
checkSubset invariant checksNames "Labels, calls, and values a step names exist, `set` changes only mutable lets, and a label's steps are together"
checkSubset typeParameter none
checkSubset input source String borrowed
checkSubset input words syntax.Words borrowed
checkSubset input rows syntax.Rows borrowed
checkSubset input entities model.Entities borrowed
checkSubset input names model.EntityNames borrowed
checkSubset input values Values borrowedMutable
checkSubset input calls Calls borrowedMutable
checkSubset input labels Labels borrowedMutable
checkSubset input steps Steps borrowedMutable
checkSubset output none
checkSubset outputOwnedBy none
checkSubset raises syntax.Rejection
checkSubset effect none
checkSubset uses none
checkSubset memoryHeap true
checkSubset async false
checkSubset maxRecursion none
checkSubset label begin loopKind none
checkSubset label begin within none
checkSubset label mainFound loopKind none
checkSubset label mainFound within none
checkSubset label eachEntity loopKind forEach
checkSubset label eachEntity within none
checkSubset label eachEntity maxIterations entityCount
checkSubset label eachEntity over entities
